title Season G fifteenth rung — the signed carry, first composition over the GREEN primitives
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first past BUHR — Rye prioritized, Glow on green-witnessed Rye; read REMEMBER, the 1024-round itinerary, the six-season double-seat, and the rye-first crypto parity wave; send each finished increment to origin and xykj61; stop at custody gates.
think Compass walk: the living edge is Season G (Cryptography). X25519 closed the fourteenth rung and the prior loop recorded that the full Monocypher-parity PRIMITIVE set is complete — no primitive remains to author. Its own recommend line named the next crux: a Kumara-facing signed/keyed carry composed over the GREEN primitives. The decision wave doc names the same thread as the Lotus unblock — "once a Rye signing primitive is parity-GREEN, Lotus's 'who made this record' signed carry becomes buildable; the library is engineering, signing with the maintainer's own identity key stays the custody gate." The 1024-round itinerary's Season 2 Journey 6 (Provenance) names the same shape: a content-addressed chain of custody.
think Lindy-first crux-first: a provenance frame serves EVERY module that records who made something — Kumara identity, Lotus signed carry, Vault, Comlink, Tablecloth-keyed artifacts — the highest-Lindy new thread once the primitives stand, and it is agent-doable (a TEST seed is not a key; the frame is held in memory, sent nowhere). The crux is de-risked because it authors NO new cryptography: it is pure composition over two already-parity-GREEN primitives (BLAKE2b-512 for the content address, Ed25519 sign/verify for the seal).
think Design (self-approved): a flat self-describing frame magic GSC1 | signer pubkey(32) | paylen(u64 big-endian, wire width per TAME) | payload | BLAKE2b-512 digest(64) | Ed25519 signature-over-digest(64). Signing the DIGEST rather than the raw payload makes the digest do double duty — it is both the content address a keeper cites and the exact value the signature commits to, so "this key vouches for this content address" is one verification, not two. The signer key lives inside the preimage, so a forger cannot swap a key without breaking the content address the real signature commits to.
think seal() builds the frame in place in the caller's out buffer (header+payload first, then hash those bytes, then sign the digest) — no second scratch buffer, allocation-free, bounded (payload <= 64 KiB keeps the preimage far inside BLAKE2b's 1 MiB bound so the digest step can never refuse, catch unreachable honest). open() verifies BEFORE trust in strict order: magic, then declared length, then a RECOMPUTED digest (a byte moved anywhere upstream is refused here, before the signature is consulted), then the signature — only then does one zero-copy payload byte leave the door, returned as a slice into the caller's frame alongside the verified signer key.
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal pass — no correction needed. Ten selftest blocks: round-trip across eight payload lengths (empty through the 64 KiB max), byte-identical determinism (Ed25519 is deterministic), an independent BLAKE2b + primitive-verify cross-check from outside seal/open, and seven refusals each caught by its OWN named error. The two failure PATHS are proven distinct: a flipped payload / spliced digest / swapped signer byte all fail DigestMismatch (the content-address gate fires first), while a flipped SIGNATURE byte leaves the digest intact and so reaches the signature gate to fail BadSignature. Plus bad magic, a too-short frame, a declared-length mismatch, and an undersized output buffer.
obs tame_style_check bans clean; crypto/signed_carry.rye lands in none of the ratchet lists (no fn past 70 lines, >=2 invariants per fn, opening triad present, snake_case, no bare copy/assert bans). Honest scope held: purely local over a TEST seed — no real identity key, no network, no funds, no real device. Constant-time timing-safety stays the Season's named horizon (it lives unchanged in the signing primitive this composes), and sealing a record with the maintainer's own identity key stays the custody gate. No gate crossed.
loom witness=crypto_signed_carry_selftest primitives_composed=2 payload_lengths=8 refusal_paths=7 result=GREEN
file crypto/signed_carry.rye the signed carry authored in pure Rye — pure composition over GREEN BLAKE2b-512 and Ed25519, verify-before-trust, GREEN on first metal pass
